<title>PANAMA: Panama, Peru sign open skies aviation agreement.</title>
<headline>Panama, Peru sign open skies aviation agreement.</headline>
<dateline>PANAMA CITY 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Panama and Peru have reached an open-skies aviation agreement, the first between two Latin American countries, Panamanian authorities said Thursday.</p>
<p>The pact, signed Wednesday in Panama City, allows the airlines of both countries to operate without restriction to and beyond each other's countries, according to a communique released by Panama's Civil Aeronautical Department (DAC).</p>
<p>The pact would eventually lead to lower fares for passengers and cargo, the communique said.</p>
<p>Panama earlier this month reached a similar open-skies agreement with the United States, the first for the United States in Latin America.</p>
<p>((-- Laurens Grant, Panama City newsroom, 507 2237739))</p>
